{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 17,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.05,
            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.089,
            0.272,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": "We have,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.426,
            0.108,
            0.581,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{AB} = \\mathrm{AC}   ( given )",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.127,
            0.707,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": "∠ADB = ∠ADC = 90° (from construction)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.146,
            0.793,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": "AD is a common side of the two triangles $\\Delta \\mathrm { A D B }$ and $\\Delta \\mathrm { A D C }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.362,
            0.171,
            0.635,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.316,
            0.847,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "Thus, the triangles satisfy the RHS condition. Hence, $\\Delta  ADB \\cong \\Delta  ADC$ This shows that $\\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{C},$ as they are corresponding parts of congruent triangles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.373,
            0.662,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": "Thus, the angles opposite to equal sides are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.402,
            0.546,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": "Can you use this fact to find $\\angle \\mathrm { B }$ and $\\angle C ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.442,
            0.563,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": "**Angles in an Equilateral Triangle**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.468,
            0.845,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": "Equilateral triangles are those in which all the sides have equal lengths."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.497,
            0.513,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": "What can we say about their angles?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.53,
            0.846,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": "We can use the recently discovered fact that angles opposite to equal sides are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.39,
            0.569,
            0.607,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.722,
            0.572,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": "The sides AB and AC are equal. $\\mathrm{SO} \\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{C}.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.391,
            0.747,
            0.608,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_15.jpg"
        },
